# S1: one menu session through every accelerator. The 2D demo (UP wraps to the
# last entry) runs on G1, is switched to the CPU path and back; the 3D demo (one
# UP) runs on G2, changes shader and restarts; the digit screen (one more UP)
# draws a 20-cell vertical stroke and classifies it on SIMD4; then the 2D demo
# runs again after both other engines have been used. Every frame is checked
# against the pinned references on the emulator and the RTL.
frame 1 down UP
frame 2 up UP
frame 2 down ENTER
frame 3 up ENTER
frame 4 down SPACE
frame 5 up SPACE
frame 6 down SPACE
frame 7 up SPACE
frame 8 down ESCAPE
frame 9 up ESCAPE
frame 9 down UP
frame 10 up UP
frame 10 down ENTER
frame 11 up ENTER
frame 13 down SPACE
frame 14 up SPACE
frame 15 down R
frame 16 up R
frame 17 down ESCAPE
frame 18 up ESCAPE
frame 18 down UP
frame 19 up UP
frame 19 down ENTER
frame 20 up ENTER
# Ten cells up from the centre, then paint twenty cells down: a stroke about as
# tall as the digits the model was trained on (docs/planning/digit-size-fix.md).
frame 21 down UP
frame 71 up UP
frame 72 down SPACE
frame 73 down DOWN
frame 173 up DOWN
frame 174 up SPACE
frame 175 down ENTER
frame 176 up ENTER
frame 178 down ESCAPE
frame 179 up ESCAPE
frame 179 down DOWN
frame 180 up DOWN
frame 180 down DOWN
frame 181 up DOWN
frame 181 down ENTER
frame 182 up ENTER
frame 184 down ESCAPE
frame 185 up ESCAPE
frame 185 down Q
